# Copy to .env and fill in.
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_api_key_here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Discord bot (only needed for discord_bot.py)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Token from: Discord Developer Portal -> your app -> Bot -> Reset Token.
# The same token is shown ONCE, so copy it immediately.
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=your_bot_token_here

# WHOULD BE ALLOWED to make the bot run a tool. This matters more than it looks:
# the review tools log into chess.com as you and launch a real Chromium on this
# machine, and a review takes 30s-2min. Comma-separated numeric user IDs.
# Find yours: Discord -> User Settings -> Advanced -> enable Developer Mode,
# then right-click yourself -> Copy User ID.
#   leave blank / unset = refuse everyone (the safe default)
#   all                  = open it to anyone who can see the bot (on purpose)
DISCORD_ALLOWED_USER_IDS=your_numeric_user_id
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# gemini-2.5-flash is gated to API keys that have used it before, so a new key
# gets 404 "no longer available". Good choices:
#   gemini-3.5-flash-lite  cheap, stable, plenty for this project (default)
#   gemini-3.1-flash-lite  cheap, strong
#   gemini-3.8-flash       current flagship: best, slowest, priciest
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite

# Optional. How many user turns one conversation keeps before the agent starts
# a fresh one. Gemini chat history cannot be truncated, so without this a
# long-lived bot would carry an entire old conversation forever -- paying for
# it and being distracted by it. The bot says when it resets, so this is
# visible rather than silent.
# AGENT_MAX_TURNS=12

# Optional. Show why the review pipeline degraded instead of swallowing it.
# debug | info | warning | error   (default: warning)
# CHESS_AGENT_LOG=debug

# Optional. 0 shows the browser window so you can solve a Cloudflare check by
# hand. 1 (default) runs in the background.
# REVIEW_HEADLESS=0

# Optional. The browser window the review runs in. This is the main lever on how
# wide a screenshot ends up: the board is height-constrained, so a shorter
# window means a smaller board and a narrower frame. Default 1400x820, which
# puts a board+panel frame at roughly 1150px instead of 1480px.
# Do not go below 1200x700 -- chess.com reflows and stops placing the review
# panel beside the board.
# REVIEW_VIEWPORT_W=1400
# REVIEW_VIEWPORT_H=820

# Optional. What goes in a review screenshot:
#   board_sidebar (default) the chessboard plus the review panel
#   board               just the chessboard
#   sidebar             just the review panel
# The left navigation is always excluded. The board is picked as a *square*
# (within 1%), so the nameplate/clock column around it is left out too.
# REVIEW_SHOT_REGION=board_sidebar

# Optional. Margin in pixels around that region. Small on purpose -- a generous
# margin just brings the page background back in. 0 for flush.
# REVIEW_SHOT_PADDING=12

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The interactive browser session
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One chess.com page stays open between calls so you can walk through a game a
# move at a time. How long it may sit unused before closing itself. 90s is long
# enough for a short conversation ("go forward", "screenshot that", "step back
# two") and short enough that a forgotten session does not hold a Chromium.
# Set it to 0 for no timeout.
# SESSION_IDLE_SECONDS=90

# Optional. How many tool round-trips one turn may take. The interactive tools
# make a SEQUENCE -- open the page, step, screenshot, read the engine -- so the
# old default of 6 cut off most interactive requests before they answered. A
# turn stopped mid-sequence is worse than a slow one: you get "stopped without a
# final answer" and a browser part-way through your game.
# AGENT_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS=12

# Optional. Ceiling on screenshots attached per turn. Discord also budgets
# uploads by bytes, so that is the limit that actually stops a flood.
# AGENT_MAX_ARTIFACTS=80

# Optional. Where the logged-in session lives. storage_state.json contains a
# live chess.com ACCESS_TOKEN + PHPSESSID -- anyone holding the file has the
# account. Point this outside the project folder to keep it out of zips and
# backups. Default: ./storage_state.json
# CHESS_AGENT_STATE=%LOCALAPPDATA%\chess-agent\storage_state.json
